L	Sentinel	Forerunner machines left behind to guard their installations, firing a continuous beam. Some carry shields. They know humans for what they are: the Forerunners' descendants, heirs to everything the machines were built to keep. So the Sentinels stand with humanity, against the Flood and the Covenant alike.
L	SentinelConstructor	A little Forerunner builder drone, made to weld and mend the installation, not to fight. Sent against intruders it does what it knows: it darts in out of nowhere, rams them, and burns at them with its cutting beam. It cannot take much punishment.
L	SentinelCrawler	A Forerunner machine that walks instead of flying, scuttling across the floor on its legs. It keeps a beam for range and lunges at anything that gets close.
L	SentinelDragoon	A long, T-shaped Forerunner gunship with a heavy shield. It carries the Enforcer's needle cannon, raking an area with strings of hard-light bolts from range, and a heavy beam gun under its nose that burns in long bursts at the same time.
L	SentinelEliminator	A Sentinel built for the purge's hardest work: a shield bubble around its hull and a beam that burns far hotter than the common Sentinel's. When one joins the fight, whatever it is burning does not last long.
L	SentinelEnforcer	A heavy Forerunner war machine that floats on hover jets. Two energy shields across its front stop anything fired from ahead; it answers with long strings of needle bolts from both arms, salvoes of homing hard-light rockets, and its claws for anything that gets close. Its back and sides are bare, so it keeps its shields turned toward the fight.
L	SentinelGold	A Sentinel cast in gold, burning a cold blue beam instead of the usual one. Majors are tougher, and the Shielded models carry an energy shield that has to be stripped first.
L	SentinelInterceptor	A slim, fast attack drone that fires needle bolts as it swoops. It cannot take much punishment, so it relies on speed, striking before its target can turn.
L	SentinelKnight	A Forerunner war machine of hard light, built around a burning core. A Knight fights with the weapon that forms its right forearm and the blade on its left, and when its shield fails it sinks into the ground in a flash of light and rises again somewhere else, often right beside its foe.
L	SentinelKnightCommander	A gold-plated Knight commander with a warm-burning core: the toughest of its kind, with a heavy shield.
L	SentinelKnightMajor	A seasoned Knight with a stronger shield and more armour.
L	SentinelKnightMinor	The common Knight, plated in grey, its core burning a cold colour.
L	SentinelLancer	A Forerunner burner. It flies in close and sprays fire across whatever it finds, which makes it deadly in tight corridors and easy prey at range.
L	SentinelMarauder	A cross-winged Forerunner raider with a standard beam. It is light and quick, meant to harass rather than hold a line.
L	SentinelOnyx	A dark Forerunner drone of a different make, compact and heavily shielded, with a blue beam. It is slow to kill and quick to punish any foe that stands in the open.
L	SentinelProtector	A light escort drone with the Enforcer's needle cannon. On its own it is no great threat, but its hard-light bolts add up fast when it flies with others.
L	SentinelSoldier	The heaviest of the new Forerunner guardians: a broad, armoured hull with a strong shield and three beams: its own, and one from a gun on either side of the hull, each firing on its own. It takes a sustained effort to bring one down, and it soaks up fire the whole while.
L	SentinelWarden	A well-shielded guardian of the installation, built to hold ground. Its beam is the common Sentinel's; its staying power is not.
